# Open Builder (`eyevinn-open-builder`)

Elevate your Claude AI experience with Open Builder's intuitive web interface. Streamline interactions, control permissions, and maintain session continuity effortlessly. Simple deployment with Docker!

[Source](https://github.com/Eyevinn/open-builder)

## Example

```terraform
resource "osc_instance" "example" {
  service_id = "eyevinn-open-builder"
  name       = "mybuilder"

  sensitive_parameters = {
    AnthropicApiKey = var.anthropic_api_key
    OscAccessToken = var.osc_access_token
  }
}
```

Commented lines are optional parameters. Values marked `"..."` need a real value. Outputs are `url`, `external_ip`, `external_port` and the raw `instance` document, see the `osc_instance` resource.

## Parameters

| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `AnthropicApiKey` | string | yes | Anthropic API key used server-side by Open Builder to call Claude (create it in the Anthropic Console, format sk-ant-...). Maps to ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; required, and the key is never exposed to the browser. Sensitive, set it in `sensitive_parameters`. |
| `OscAccessToken` | string | no | Personal Access Token for Open Source Cloud, obtained in the OSC web console. Maps to OSC_ACCESS_TOKEN and is needed for the deployment features that publish generated sites to OSC; optional otherwise. Sensitive, set it in `sensitive_parameters`. |

The instance `name` must match `^\w+$` and be unique per service within the workspace. OSC lowercases it and allows at most 20 characters.

Parameter values are strings; booleans take `"true"` or `"false"`. Reference an `osc_secret` as `osc_secret.<name>.ref` to keep a value out of the instance configuration. This page is generated from the OSC catalog; the provider validates against the live catalog when planning.
